1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:02,359
Nosebleed: head back or head forward?

2
00:00:02,359 --> 00:00:03,898
Many people get this wrong.

3
00:00:05,750 --> 00:00:09,526
Most nosebleeds come from tiny blood vessels in the front of the nose.

4
00:00:11,250 --> 00:00:14,727
1 — Sit up and lean forward, so blood doesn't run down your throat.

5
00:00:16,250 --> 00:00:20,325
2 — Firmly pinch the soft part of the nose, just below the bony bridge.

6
00:00:21,250 --> 00:00:23,871
3 — Hold for 10–15 minutes without letting go.

7
00:00:23,871 --> 00:00:25,410
Breathe through your mouth.

8
00:00:26,750 --> 00:00:30,675
Don't tilt your head back: blood runs down your throat and can make you vomit.

9
00:00:32,250 --> 00:00:37,925
Get urgent care if it lasts 20+ minutes with pressure, follows a head injury, or is very heavy.
